{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness","id":726392,"title":"Alertness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-25T10:09:59-07:00","id":726392,"title":"Alertness","content":"How many of you use Perception + Alertness for everything visual? I know it's intended for tactical use primarily but we default to it for everything from detecting surprise to searching a room. Is this the common use for your games as well, or do you require the Search skill instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:03:42-07:00","id":726689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness#post726392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of you use Perception + Alertness for everything visual? I know it's intended for tactical use primarily but we default to it for everything from detecting surprise to searching a room. Is this the common use for your games as well, or do you require the Search skill instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh? Why would be only visual or tactical?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alertness describes the attention that the character pays<br /> to the world around him, whether he\u2019s actively looking or<br /> not. It measures how attuned the character is to things that<br /> he can see, smell, hear, and touch \u2014 and to the less tangible<br /> conclusions that come from his senses. In combat, it\u2019s often<br /> paired with Wits to gauge a character\u2019s reaction time and<br /> ability to respond; out of combat, it\u2019s most usually paired with<br /> Perception to gain clues about a character\u2019s surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:30:32-07:00","id":726885,"title":"","content":"I tend to use investigate + perception/intelligence if they are doing fine-tooth comb searches or professional inspections of crime scenes. Being generally perceptive does not necessarily make you Sherlock Holmes or a trained crime scene investigator.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:33:13-07:00","id":726896,"title":"","content":"Alertness is pretty much the default &quot;do I notice something&quot; Ability regardless of context. It's other Abilities that intrude on Alertness in specialized situations (ex: Investigation takes over for a thorough examination of a room compared to spotting a quick clue).<br /> <br /> I actually really dislike Alertness on a conceptual level, but Cogliostro hit it on the head for RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T15:18:39-07:00","id":727147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness?p=726896#post726896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alertness is pretty much the default &quot;do I notice something&quot; Ability regardless of context. It's other Abilities that intrude on Alertness in specialized situations (ex: Investigation takes over for a thorough examination of a room compared to spotting a quick clue).<br /> <br /> I actually really dislike Alertness on a conceptual level, but Cogliostro hit it on the head for RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is more how I should have phrased my questions as this better describes how we use it. I get the idea that it is mostly a tactical skill from the fact that suggested specializations are directed that way. At least in the Mage books they are. <br /> <br /> As for Investigation, we use it for noticing things that can be tied to a scene that though they might be noticed (through Alertness) they don't appear to have any relevance. The Search skill is what our group tends to lump in with Alertness, to the point that we have pretty much made Search a specialization of Alertness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T01:55:59-07:00","id":728174,"title":"","content":"The M20 specialties for Alertness have a good number of non-tactical or at least not exclusive tactical options.<br /> <br /> Search is a secondary Ability that's pretty much &quot;Investigation for people that can't justify normal Investigation for some reason.&quot; I've never used it, and I've never seen a need for it, which is fortunate since secondaries are generally optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T22:06:58-07:00","id":731254,"title":"","content":"The only downside to Investigate is it can't be used untrained, so I usually allow perception + alertness for &quot;searching for clues&quot; (and all seeing/hearing checks) and investigate gets a lower difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T14:11:39-07:00","id":733084,"title":"","content":"Awareness would apply rather than Alertness if there's something supernatural or otherworldly to notice, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:53:34-07:00","id":734450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness?p=733084#post733084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awareness would apply rather than Alertness if there's something supernatural or otherworldly to notice, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T14:03:20-07:00","id":735751,"title":"","content":"Assuming you're running a game that uses Awareness (as not all of them do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:22:13-07:00","id":742864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness?p=731254#post731254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only downside to Investigate is it can't be used untrained, so I usually allow perception + alertness for &quot;searching for clues&quot; (and all seeing/hearing checks) and investigate gets a lower difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their in an of itself is the problem with your issue. Break up what they do and make people spend points elsewhere if they want to do stuff that is that skill/knowledge. You don't have it, no investigating for you. There, alertness not used for everything. *mind exploded I know*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T14:51:53-07:00","id":742964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/726392-alertness#post726392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of you use Perception + Alertness for everything visual? I know it's intended for tactical use primarily but we default to it for everything from detecting surprise to searching a room. Is this the common use for your games as well, or do you require the Search skill instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per another further up response, I think you are having a slightly skewed perspective of the Ability, hence the slightly weird nature of your question. Alertness is used for noticing anything immediate in the character's sensory range, not merely visual and certainly not just tactical. A character rolling Perception+Alertness could be doing so to notice: a shadow shifting in his peripheral vision; the slight scent of something burning in the kitchen/in a nearby yard; to feel something small (like a spider) crawling up his arm/back/what-have-you; to notice the slight shift in tone of the many screaming kids on the playground wherein one of the children is crying &quot;for real&quot; because they've been legitimately hurt; discerning that the slightly flat soda he just sipped has an usual -- if subtle -- acidity to it... possibly noting that he's been slipped something in his drink. It can be for any of those things and more, so long as said sensory input is within the normal range for his sense (which may, of course, be abnormal by human standards via certain Merits, magic, what-have-you).<br /> <br /> As for searching for things, a Perception+Alertness roll may be useful for general spotting of this, that and the other when searching a room (especially, and more specifically, when a noted thing in particular is being looked for). Investigation, however, is the ability to be used in order to key together aspects of what is perceived in a manner that provides information beyond the obvious (or even not-so-obvious). Examples: Alertness may let the character note that there is some dust on the floor that is out-of-place with what is around it; Investigation would reveal that the dust isn't from within the room, or likely even the house, and subtle patterning in part of the dust denotes it as probably having been left behind by someone's shoes/footsteps... shoes with soles that are considerably worn. Similarly, Alertness might let you find a particular book among hundreds/thousands that are scattered in a given study... but Investigation would help the character note (when paired with Intelligence) that *other* books *not* being searched for that are in the piles are a clue to the mindset of the owner in question, even as the searching character may not have been looking for &quot;x&quot; other books.<br /> <br /> It's a subtle distinction for some people, but Alertness, Awareness and Investigation are well-split in terms of what they cover/are used for. (Sure, some people go the much more specific route of using Search, Spot, Research and similar, and that's fine for those who want to be more specific about character qualities; I, though, and virtually everyone I've ever gamed with over the past 3 decades, rarely go that far as it creates needless point counting. WoD, in whatever incarnation, is generally supposed to be played more intuitively and on a comparatively &quot;simpler&quot; mechanical level than, say, DnD 3.0/3.5, which is stat'd-the-house-down. Still, though -- to each their own.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}